17:06:50 INFO    C2: Use the most-worn valid location with robust levelling: 16 runs measurable with an LOD, replicate SD 0.07 dex, Archard R² P1 +0.29 / P2 +0.15; the old mean-of-locations, plain-levelling measure gives 0.34 dex and R² +0.08 / +0.01. Exponents: V ~ L^0.96 [0.41, 1.59] S^-0.07 [-1.32, 1.61] (Archard: 1, 1). The TA depth rule scores a higher R² (+0.52) only because it drops the shallow part of every groove: runs at <= 25 N keep a median 11 % of their groove, runs at >= 60 N 91 %, which inflates the load exponent to 1.9; it is not a volume.
17:09:13 INFO    C3: COF first 10 s: final = physics law (selected ML: ANN + physics); COF end: final = physics law (selected ML: none); log10 V: final = physics law (selected ML: ANN); log10 width: final = physics law (selected ML: GPR + physics); log10 k: final = physics law (selected ML: ANN + physics).
